  "id": "COMPOUND:22331 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Acorone is implicated in the relationship with Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through a chain of targets that ultimately leads to this protein. The evidence suggests that Acorone acts as a target of two distinct compounds: Sodium/bile acid cotransporter and Trichosanthoside A. Both of these compounds are known to interact with Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving this protein. The presence of multiple targets that share a common downstream effect on Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit suggests a possible role in the regulation or modulation of this protein. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the sodium/bile acid cotransporter and Trichosanthoside A in the biological context of Acorone's activity, reinforcing the notion that Acorone may influence Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through these intermediaries.",
